{"type":"message","id":"abaa0cda","parentId":"e8a58dff","timestamp":"2026-05-22T23:36:13.806Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN is asking why the resume/restore doesn't read memory files anymore. Let me think about this...\n\nThe current `session_manager.py resume` restores:\n- Summary\n- Messages (last N)\n- Keywords\n\nBut the original AGENTS.md \"Every Session\" step 6 was:\n```\npython3 restore.py auto\n```\n\nAnd the restore.py auto does:\n1. Read .last_session_id\n2. Restore session data (summary + messages + keywords)\n3. Print the context\n\nBut VAN is pointing out that the resume doesn't read MEMORY.md or memory/*.md files. The original design in AGENTS.md steps 1-5 reads SOUL.md, USER.md, IDENTITY.md, memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md, and MEMORY.md. Step 6 is the session restore.\n\n\nSo the resume only recovers session-specific data, but the broader memory context—like long-term preferences and accumulated knowledge from MEMORY.md and the daily memory files—isn't being loaded during the restore process. That's the gap VAN is identifying.\n\nThe cleanest fix would be to have `session_manager.py resume` automatically load MEMORY.md and today's memory file after restoring the session, so the agent gets both the session context and the accumulated memory context in one flow.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"好问题。`resume` 只恢复了会话数据（摘要+消息+关键词），没有读 MEMORY.md 和 memory/*.md。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01abb4d114ec46b69b7ed172","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/workspace/projects/workspace/skills/hermes-skills/hermes-sync-core/session_manager.py","limit":50,"offset":230}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":34873,"output":601,"cacheRead":28672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64146,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779492964477}}
